          "prediction": "China is at the forefront of global patenting activity in low-emission energy sources for heavy-duty vehicles (Figure 3.5). Between 2000 and 2024, China was responsible for almost 17,400 published patent families, based on inventor addresses on published patents. However, it is noteworthy that only 10% of all Chinese patents belong to international patent families with protection extended to two or more countries. This percentage is lower than in all other leading countries. The huge domestic market in China means that many Chinese companies do focus solely on their domestic market and therefore only seek patent protection there. As a result, their inventions are legally protected only within China, which can limit the companies’ ability to expand internationally."
